      <main id="content"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianLipschitzExponential.integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h1>Gaussian Lipschitz first moment and signed exponential domain</h1><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianLipschitzExponential.integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For every actual Gaussian mu and globally L-Lipschitz scalar f on the stated Banach/Borel space, f is Bochner integrable and exp(t*(f-int f dmu)) is integrable for every real t. This is a Gaussian-domain background theorem, not the sharp concentration bound.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[f\in L^1(\mu),\qquad e^{t(f-\int f\,d\mu)}\in L^1(\mu)\quad(t\in\mathbb R).\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Produce the genuine first moment</strong><p>Lipschitz growth bounds the actual scalar observable by L times the norm plus its value at zero. Gaussian first Bochner integrability from pinned Mathlib yields norm L1. Continuity gives measurability, so domination yields scalar L1 and a genuine finite mean.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Use actual Fernique integrability</strong><p>Pinned Gaussian Fernique gives one actual C&gt;0 with exp(C norm(x)^2) integrable. The space is a complete second-countable real Banach Borel space. The Gaussian need not be centered or nondegenerate; zero dimensions and zero Lipschitz constant require no extra branch or premise.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Dominate every signed centered exponential</strong><p>For each real t set b=abs(t)L and D=abs(t)(abs(f(0))+abs(m)). Young inequality gives b norm(x)&lt;=C norm(x)^2+C^-1 b^2. Thus the centered exponential is dominated by a finite scalar times the genuine Fernique integrand. This proves the domain only; its constant depends on C and f(0), and supplies no sharp concentration coefficient.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>Real complete second-countable normed vector space E with Borel measurable structure, Gaussian probability measure mu (possibly noncentered/degenerate).</li><li>Actual globally Lipschitz scalar function f:E-&gt;R with NNReal constant L, including L=0. No differentiability, boundedness, positive dimension, given mean, Laplace certificate or sharp coefficient premise.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Produce the genuine first moment</h4><p>Lipschitz growth bounds the actual scalar observable by L times the norm plus its value at zero. Gaussian first Bochner integrability from pinned Mathlib yields norm L1. Continuity gives measurability, so domination yields scalar L1 and a genuine finite mean.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[|f(x)|\le L\|x\|+|f(0)|,\quad f\in L^1(\mu),\quad m=\int f\,d\mu.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>IsGaussian.integrable_id; LipschitzWith.dist_le_mul; Integrable.mono&#x27;</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Use actual Fernique integrability</h4><p>Pinned Gaussian Fernique gives one actual C&gt;0 with exp(C norm(x)^2) integrable. The space is a complete second-countable real Banach Borel space. The Gaussian need not be centered or nondegenerate; zero dimensions and zero Lipschitz constant require no extra branch or premise.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\exists C&gt;0:\quad\int e^{C\|x\|^2}\,d\mu(x)&lt;\infty.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>ProbabilityTheory.IsGaussian.exists_integrable_exp_sq</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Dominate every signed centered exponential</h4><p>For each real t set b=abs(t)L and D=abs(t)(abs(f(0))+abs(m)). Young inequality gives b norm(x)&lt;=C norm(x)^2+C^-1 b^2. Thus the centered exponential is dominated by a finite scalar times the genuine Fernique integrand. This proves the domain only; its constant depends on C and f(0), and supplies no sharp concentration coefficient.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[b=|t|L,\ D=|t|(|f(0)|+|m|),\quad e^{t(f(x)-m)}\le e^{D+C^{-1}b^2}e^{C\|x\|^2}.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>two_mul_le_add_mul_sq; Real.exp_le_exp; Integrable.const_mul; Integrable.mono&#x27;</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianLipschitzExponential.integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz"><summary>Lean statement · integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz</summary><p>For every actual Gaussian mu and globally L-Lipschitz scalar f on the stated Banach/Borel space, f is Bochner integrable and exp(t*(f-int f dmu)) is integrable for every real t. This is a Gaussian-domain background theorem, not the sharp concentration bound.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [SecondCountableTopology E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E} [ProbabilityTheory.IsGaussian μ]
    {L : ℝ≥0} {f : E → ℝ} (hf : LipschitzWith L f) :
    MeasureTheory.Integrable f μ ∧ ∀ t : ℝ,
      MeasureTheory.Integrable
        (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (t * (f x - ∫ z, f z ∂μ))) μ</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-probability-gaussianlipschitzexponential.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianLipschitzExponential.integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz"><summary>Lean proof · integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz</summary><p>Produce the genuine first moment; Use actual Fernique integrability; Dominate every signed centered exponential</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [SecondCountableTopology E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E} [ProbabilityTheory.IsGaussian μ]
    {L : ℝ≥0} {f : E → ℝ} (hf : LipschitzWith L f) :
    MeasureTheory.Integrable f μ ∧ ∀ t : ℝ,
      MeasureTheory.Integrable
        (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (t * (f x - ∫ z, f z ∂μ))) μ := by
  have hbound (x : E) : |f x| ≤ (L : ℝ)*‖x‖+|f 0| := by
    have hd := hf.dist_le_mul x 0
    simp only [dist_eq_norm, sub_zero, Real.norm_eq_abs] at hd
    calc
      |f x| = |(f x-f 0)+f 0| := by congr 1; ring
      _ ≤ |f x-f 0|+|f 0| := abs_add_le _ _
      _ ≤ (L : ℝ)*‖x‖+|f 0| := add_le_add hd le_rfl
  have hi : Integrable f μ :=
    (((IsGaussian.integrable_id (μ := μ)).norm.const_mul (L : ℝ)).add
      (integrable_const |f 0|)).mono&#x27; hf.continuous.aestronglyMeasurable
        (ae_of_all _ fun x =&gt; by simpa only [Real.norm_eq_abs, Pi.add_apply, id_eq] using hbound x)
  refine ⟨hi,fun t =&gt; ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨C,hC,hint⟩ := IsGaussian.exists_integrable_exp_sq μ
  let b : ℝ := |t| *(L : ℝ)
  let D : ℝ := |t| *(|f 0|+|∫ z, f z ∂μ|)
  have hb : 0 ≤ b := mul_nonneg (abs_nonneg _) L.coe_nonneg
  have hdom (x : E) : t*(f x-∫ z, f z ∂μ) ≤
      D+C⁻¹*b^2+C*‖x‖^2 := by
    have hlin : t*(f x-∫ z, f z ∂μ) ≤ b*‖x‖+D := by
      calc
        _ ≤ |t*(f x-∫ z, f z ∂μ)| := le_abs_self _
        _ = |t| *|f x-∫ z, f z ∂μ| := abs_mul _ _
        _ ≤ |t| *(|f x|+|∫ z, f z ∂μ|) :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (by simpa only [sub_zero, zero_sub, abs_neg] using
            (abs_sub_le (f x) 0 (∫ z, f z ∂μ))) (abs_nonneg _)
        _ ≤ |t| *((L : ℝ)*‖x‖+|f 0|+|∫ z, f z ∂μ|) :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (add_le_add (hbound x) le_rfl) (abs_nonneg _)
        _ = b*‖x‖+D := by dsimp [b,D]; ring
    have hy : 2*‖x‖*b ≤ C*‖x‖^2+C⁻¹*b^2 := two_mul_le_add_mul_sq hC
    have hnon : 0 ≤ b*‖x‖ := mul_nonneg hb (norm_nonneg _)
    nlinarith
  apply (hint.const_mul (Real.exp (D+C⁻¹*b^2))).mono&#x27;
    (by fun_prop)
  filter_upwards with x
  rw [Real.norm_eq_abs,abs_of_pos (Real.exp_pos _),← Real.exp_add]
  exact Real.exp_le_exp.mpr (hdom x)

end AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianLipschitzExponential
end</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-probability-gaussianlipschitzexponential.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Genuine Gaussian-gradient-output first Bochner moment and every signed directional centered exponential L1, plus existing exact positive-step proximal/input/noise semantics only. Sharp centered coefficient eta*normu^2/2 in4.3, bias4.2, FIRSTW2/LSI/T2/fullLemma4.2, posterior jointkernel/higher smoothing/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization/main/work/composition remainOPEN. Domain proof is authored Fernique alternative, not Gaussian concentration constant. TV never transfers unboundedcost. Exactstatements/topology alreadysealed beforeproof; no unreviewed signature gap.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><ul><li>ProbabilityTheory.IsGaussian.integrable_id</li><li>ProbabilityTheory.IsGaussian.exists_integrable_exp_sq</li><li>LipschitzWith.dist_le_mul</li><li>Integrable.mono&#x27;</li><li>two_mul_le_add_mul_sq</li></ul><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d/Mathlib/Probability/Distributions/Gaussian/Fernique.lean">Pinned Gaussian domain background</a> — Genuine Gaussian-gradient-output first Bochner moment and every signed directional centered exponential L1, plus existing exact positive-step proximal/input/noise semantics only. Sharp centered coefficient eta*normu^2/2 in4.3, bias4.2, FIRSTW2/LSI/T2/fullLemma4.2, posterior jointkernel/higher smoothing/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization/main/work/composition remainOPEN. Domain proof is authored Fernique alternative, not Gaussian concentration constant. TV never transfers unboundedcost. Exactstatements/topology alreadysealed beforeproof; no unreviewed signature gap.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></main>
